From: NanoKVM OS <nanokvm@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] _ssl: do not reference removed OpenSSL 4 version methods

OpenSSL 4 no longer exports SSLv3_method, TLSv1_method,
TLSv1_1_method, or TLSv1_2_method. Its headers do not currently define
all of the corresponding feature macros, so CPython emits unresolved
references or fails while compiling the target _ssl module.

The generic TLS, TLS client, and TLS server methods remain available.
Disable only the removed, already deprecated fixed-version protocols.

Upstream: Not submitted
---
 Modules/_ssl.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Modules/_ssl.c b/Modules/_ssl.c
--- a/Modules/_ssl.c
+++ b/Modules/_ssl.c
@@ -73,6 +73,13 @@
 #include "openssl/bio.h"
 #include "openssl/dh.h"
 
+#if OPENSSL_VERSION_MAJOR >= 4
+#  define OPENSSL_NO_SSL3 1
+#  define OPENSSL_NO_TLS1_METHOD 1
+#  define OPENSSL_NO_TLS1_1_METHOD 1
+#  define OPENSSL_NO_TLS1_2_METHOD 1
+#endif
+
 #ifndef OPENSSL_THREADS
 #  error "OPENSSL_THREADS is not defined, Python requires thread-safe OpenSSL"
 #endif
